<rules>
<rule id="3c67-4893-3aa1-a1e4" name="Allegiance" hidden="false">
<description>The army's Allegiance determines which characters, units, wargear, Rites of War and other options may be selected. A Legion is not inherently restricted to a particular Allegiance.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="fc99-c192-1312-1d61" name="Allies Matrix: Thousand Sons" hidden="false">
<description>Allies Matrix - At the Height of the Heresy. Allies and Brothers: Emperor's Children, Exercitus Imperialis, Iron Warriors, Mechanicum, Night Lords, Questoris Households, Solar Auxilia, Sons of Horus, Thousand Sons, Word Bearers, World Eaters. Conditional Alliance: Alpha Legion, Blackshields (The Lost and the Damned), Daemons of the Ruinstorm. Sworn Enemies: Blood Angels, Dark Angels, Death Guard, Imperial Fists, Iron Hands, Raven Guard, Salamanders, Space Wolves, Talons of the Emperor, Ultramarines, White Scars. Apply the chart separately to every pair of detachments in the army. An alliance never overrides army-building restrictions, allegiance requirements or the specific wording of a unit, ability or item of wargear. A Legion fielded with the other allegiance (e.g. Loyalist Sons of Horus) swaps sides: Sworn Enemies that only come from the two sides of the Heresy become allies, and all detachments of an army must share one allegiance.</description>
</rule>
</rules>
